# One line ending in the repository, whatever the checkout does locally.
#
# Without this, git on the Linux side of the Cowork bridge reports ~265 files as
# modified while Windows git (which applies core.autocrlf) reports a clean tree.
# Same working tree, two answers. The risk is not the noise, it is that a
# `git add -A` from the Linux side commits a whole-repo line-ending rewrite and
# takes `git blame` with it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the object store and leaves the working
# copy to each platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated. Keeps review diffs honest about what a human actually changed.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
